<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#A4.SS4" title="In Appendix D Theory ‣ vAttention: Verified Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">D.4 </span>Why reducing bias in estimation is more important than reducing variance.</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1" title="In D.4 Why reducing bias in estimation is more important than reducing variance. ‣ Appendix D Theory ‣ vAttention: Verified Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">case 1: Entire MSE is attributed to bias</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2" title="In D.4 Why reducing bias in estimation is more important than reducing variance. ‣ Appendix D Theory ‣ vAttention: Verified Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">case 2: Entire MSE is attributed to variance</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
