<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Achieving required sparsity.</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To achieve the required sparsity, we search for the configuration parameters on a few examples from the dataset and select the configuration with the minimum local attention approximation error while maintaining the target sparsity. The search space used is mentioned table <a href="#A1.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ A.2 Achieving required sparsity. ‣ Appendix A Additional Experiments Results and Details ‣ vAttention: Verified Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>,</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>For local and sink tokens we use fixed 128 tokens throughout experiments for all methods.</figcaption>
