<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Detailed results at 10% sparsity</h3>

<figure id="A1.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>RULER @ 32K (Meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct) at 10% sparsity full benchmark results. As mentioned in the paper, half of the datasets are quite easy and solvable by HashAttention. However, the harder datasets is where vAttention bridges the gap between full attention and HashAttention / oracle-top-<math id="A1.T4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> significantly.</figcaption>
