<div id="A3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Furthermore, some methods deliberately mix dense and sparse attention across layers. We take a different stance: sparse attention itself should be sufficiently adaptive to each layer’s requirements, increasing its effective density when necessary rather than relying on dense layers as a fallback.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Theory</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Derivation via Central Limit Theorem (CLT)</h3>

<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Estimating vector sum</span>)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{s}=\sum_{i=1}^{n_{s}}\mathbf{r}_{i},\mathbf{s}\in R^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msubsup><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{s}=\sum_{i=1}^{n_{s}}\mathbf{r}_{i},\mathbf{s}\in R^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> be a sum of <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n_{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n_{s}</annotation></semantics></math> vector quantities <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{r}_{i}\in R^{d}\,\forall i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{r}_{i}\in R^{d}\,\forall i</annotation></semantics></math> which have to be estimated using a sample <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> be the covariance matrix for the population <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathbf{r}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathbf{r}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathbf{s}}_{b}=\frac{n_{s}}{b}\left(\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{b}}\mathbf{r}_{i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>b</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathbf{s}}_{b}=\frac{n_{s}}{b}\left(\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{b}}\mathbf{r}_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> be the estimate. Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> be the CDF for the normal distribution. Then for a large enough <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> if,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\geq\left(\Phi^{-1}\left(1-\frac{\delta}{2}\right)\frac{n_{s}\sqrt{\mathbf{Tr}(\Sigma)}}{\tau}\right)^{2}\;\;\;\;\textrm{then}\;\;\;\;\mathbf{Pr}(||\hat{\mathbf{s}}-\mathbf{s}||_{2}&gt;\tau)\leq\delta" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>𝐓𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mspace style="width:1.12em;" width="1.12em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">then</mtext><mspace style="width:1.12em;" width="1.12em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐏𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\geq\left(\Phi^{-1}\left(1-\frac{\delta}{2}\right)\frac{n_{s}\sqrt{\mathbf{Tr}(\Sigma)}}{\tau}\right)^{2}\;\;\;\;\textrm{then}\;\;\;\;\mathbf{Pr}(||\hat{\mathbf{s}}-\mathbf{s}||_{2}&gt;\tau)\leq\delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for any arbitrary <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in R</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Using the Multivariate Central Limit Theorem,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{b}\,\left(\frac{1}{b}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{b}}\mathbf{r_{i}}-\frac{s}{n}\right)\;\xrightarrow{d}\;\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\bm{\Sigma})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mi>b</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>𝐢</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>s</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑑</mo></mover><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{b}\,\left(\frac{1}{b}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{b}}\mathbf{r_{i}}-\frac{s}{n}\right)\;\xrightarrow{d}\;\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\bm{\Sigma}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sqrt{b}}{n}\,\left(\frac{n}{b}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{b}}\mathbf{r_{i}}-s\right)\;\xrightarrow{d}\;\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\bm{\Sigma})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mi>b</mi></msqrt><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi>𝐫</mi><mi>𝐢</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑑</mo></mover><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sqrt{b}}{n}\,\left(\frac{n}{b}\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{b}}\mathbf{r_{i}}-s\right)\;\xrightarrow{d}\;\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\bm{\Sigma}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sqrt{b}}{n}\,\left(\mathbf{\hat{s}}-\mathbf{s}\right)\;\xrightarrow{d}\;\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\bm{\Sigma})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mi>b</mi></msqrt><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑑</mo></mover><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sqrt{b}}{n}\,\left(\mathbf{\hat{s}}-\mathbf{s}\right)\;\xrightarrow{d}\;\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\bm{\Sigma}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sqrt{b}}{n}\,\mathbf{u}^{\top}\left(\mathbf{\hat{s}}-\mathbf{s}\right)\;\xrightarrow{d}\;\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{u}^{\top}\bm{\Sigma}\mathbf{u})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msqrt><mi>b</mi></msqrt><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑑</mo></mover><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sqrt{b}}{n}\,\mathbf{u}^{\top}\left(\mathbf{\hat{s}}-\mathbf{s}\right)\;\xrightarrow{d}\;\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{u}^{\top}\bm{\Sigma}\mathbf{u}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}^{\top}\left(\mathbf{\hat{s}}-\mathbf{s}\right)\;\xrightarrow{d}\;\frac{n}{\sqrt{b}}\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{u}^{\top}\bm{\Sigma}\mathbf{u})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐬</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐬</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>→</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">𝑑</mo></mover><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><msqrt><mi>b</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}^{\top}\left(\mathbf{\hat{s}}-\mathbf{s}\right)\;\xrightarrow{d}\;\frac{n}{\sqrt{b}}\mathcal{N}(\mathbf{0},\mathbf{u}^{\top}\bm{\Sigma}\mathbf{u}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">To achieve a error within <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we must have</p>
<table id="A4.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{n}{\sqrt{b}}\sqrt{(\mathbf{u}^{\top}\bm{\Sigma}\mathbf{u})}\Phi^{-1}\left(1-\frac{\delta}{2}\right)&lt;\tau" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><msqrt><mi>b</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐮</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{n}{\sqrt{b}}\sqrt{(\mathbf{u}^{\top}\bm{\Sigma}\mathbf{u})}\Phi^{-1}\left(1-\frac{\delta}{2}\right)&lt;\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p">This can be achieved if</p>
<table id="A4.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{n}{\sqrt{b}}(\sqrt{\mathbf{Tr}}(\bm{\Sigma}))\Phi^{-1}\left(1-\frac{\delta}{2}\right)&lt;\tau" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><msqrt><mi>b</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>𝐓𝐫</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{n}{\sqrt{b}}(\sqrt{\mathbf{Tr}}(\bm{\Sigma}))\Phi^{-1}\left(1-\frac{\delta}{2}\right)&lt;\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p">Solving for <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b&gt;\left(\frac{n}{\tau}(\sqrt{\mathbf{Tr}}(\bm{\Sigma}))\Phi^{-1}\left(1-\frac{\delta}{2}\right)\right)^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>τ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>𝐓𝐫</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b&gt;\left(\frac{n}{\tau}(\sqrt{\mathbf{Tr}}(\bm{\Sigma}))\Phi^{-1}\left(1-\frac{\delta}{2}\right)\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Corollaries for Numerator and Denominator</h3>

<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{(\epsilon,\delta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{(\epsilon,\delta)}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">approximation of</span> <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐍</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{N}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma</annotation></semantics></math> be the covariance matrix for the population <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\exp{\langle K[i],q\rangle}V[i]\}_{i\in\bar{\mathcal{I}_{f}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\exp{\langle K[i],q\rangle}V[i]\}_{i\in\bar{\mathcal{I}_{f}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{N}=N_{f}+\frac{n_{s}}{b}\left(\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{dyn}}\exp{\langle K[i],q}V[i]\rangle\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>N</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{N}=N_{f}+\frac{n_{s}}{b}\left(\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{dyn}}\exp{\langle K[i],q}V[i]\rangle\right)</annotation></semantics></math> be the estimate when using sample <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{dyn}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{dyn}</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> be the CDF for the normal distribution. Then for a large enough <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> and for any arbitrary <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon,\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon,\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, if</span></p>
<table id="A4.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\geq\left(\Phi^{-1}\left(1-\frac{\delta}{2}\right)\frac{n_{s}\sqrt{\mathbf{Tr}(\Sigma)}}{\epsilon||N||_{2}}\right)^{2}\;\;\;\;\textrm{then}\;\;\;\;\mathbf{Pr}(||\hat{N}-N||_{2}&gt;\epsilon||N||_{2})\leq\delta" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>𝐓𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mspace style="width:1.12em;" width="1.12em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">then</mtext><mspace style="width:1.12em;" width="1.12em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐏𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>N</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\geq\left(\Phi^{-1}\left(1-\frac{\delta}{2}\right)\frac{n_{s}\sqrt{\mathbf{Tr}(\Sigma)}}{\epsilon||N||_{2}}\right)^{2}\;\;\;\;\textrm{then}\;\;\;\;\mathbf{Pr}(||\hat{N}-N||_{2}&gt;\epsilon||N||_{2})\leq\delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary D.3</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{(\epsilon,\delta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{(\epsilon,\delta)}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">approximation of</span> <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐃</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{D}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> be the standard deviation for the population <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\exp{K[i],q}\}_{i\in\bar{\mathcal{I}_{f}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\exp{K[i],q}\}_{i\in\bar{\mathcal{I}_{f}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{D}=D_{f}+\frac{n_{s}}{b}\left(\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{dyn}}\exp{\langle K[i],q\rangle}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>b</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{D}=D_{f}+\frac{n_{s}}{b}\left(\sum_{i\in\mathcal{I}_{dyn}}\exp{\langle K[i],q\rangle}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> be the estimate when using sample <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{dyn}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{dyn}</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi</annotation></semantics></math> be the CDF for the normal distribution. Then for a large enough <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>, for any arbitrary <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon,\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon,\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, if</span></p>
<table id="A4.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\geq\left(\Phi^{-1}\left(1-\frac{\delta}{2}\right)\frac{n_{s}\sigma}{\epsilon D}\right)^{2}\;\;\;\;\textrm{then}\;\;\;\;\mathbf{Pr}(|\hat{D}-D|&gt;\epsilon D)\leq\delta" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mspace style="width:1.12em;" width="1.12em"></mspace><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">then</mtext><mspace style="width:1.12em;" width="1.12em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐏𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\geq\left(\Phi^{-1}\left(1-\frac{\delta}{2}\right)\frac{n_{s}\sigma}{\epsilon D}\right)^{2}\;\;\;\;\textrm{then}\;\;\;\;\mathbf{Pr}(|\hat{D}-D|&gt;\epsilon D)\leq\delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Combination of approximations of numerator and denominator</h3>

<div id="A4.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.4</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> are chosen such that we have <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon_{1},\delta_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon_{1},\delta_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon_{2},\delta_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon_{2},\delta_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> approximation on numerator and denominator respectively and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{2}&lt;0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{2}&lt;0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, then using <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=\max(b_{D},b_{N})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=\max(b_{D},b_{N})</annotation></semantics></math> ensures that</span></p>
<table id="A4.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Pr}\left(\left\lVert\frac{N}{D}-\frac{\hat{N}}{\hat{D}}\right\rVert_{2}&gt;2(\epsilon_{1}+\epsilon_{2})\right)\left\lVert\frac{N}{D}\right\rVert_{2}&lt;(\delta_{1}+\delta_{2})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐏𝐫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>N</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mfrac></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Pr}\left(\left\lVert\frac{N}{D}-\frac{\hat{N}}{\hat{D}}\right\rVert_{2}&gt;2(\epsilon_{1}+\epsilon_{2})\right)\left\lVert\frac{N}{D}\right\rVert_{2}&lt;(\delta_{1}+\delta_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If we have a <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon_{1},\delta_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon_{1},\delta_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> approxiamtion for numerator and <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon_{2},\delta_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon_{2},\delta_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> for denominator. Consider the following expression</p>
<table id="A4.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle||\frac{\hat{N}}{\hat{D}}-\frac{N}{D}||_{2}=||\frac{D\hat{N}-\hat{D}N}{\hat{D}D}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>N</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>N</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle||\frac{\hat{N}}{\hat{D}}-\frac{N}{D}||_{2}=||\frac{D\hat{N}-\hat{D}N}{\hat{D}D}||</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">With probability <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\delta_{1}-\delta_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\delta_{1}-\delta_{2})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A4.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle||\frac{D\hat{N}-DN\pm\epsilon_{2}DN}{\hat{D}D}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>N</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>±</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle||\frac{D\hat{N}-DN\pm\epsilon_{2}DN}{\hat{D}D}||</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=||\frac{\hat{N}-N\pm\epsilon_{2}N}{\hat{D}}||" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>N</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>±</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=||\frac{\hat{N}-N\pm\epsilon_{2}N}{\hat{D}}||</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{||\hat{N}-N||_{2}+\epsilon_{2}||N||_{2}}{D(1\pm\epsilon_{1})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>N</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>±</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{||\hat{N}-N||_{2}+\epsilon_{2}||N||_{2}}{D(1\pm\epsilon_{1})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\epsilon_{1}||N||_{2}+\epsilon_{2}||N||_{2}}{D(1\pm\epsilon_{2})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>±</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\epsilon_{1}||N||_{2}+\epsilon_{2}||N||_{2}}{D(1\pm\epsilon_{2})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(\epsilon_{1}+\epsilon_{2})\frac{||N||_{2}}{D(1-\epsilon_{2})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(\epsilon_{1}+\epsilon_{2})\frac{||N||_{2}}{D(1-\epsilon_{2})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(\epsilon_{1}+\epsilon_{2})(1+2\epsilon_{2})\frac{||N||_{2}}{D}\;\;\textrm{ if }\epsilon_{2}&lt;0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.560em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(\epsilon_{1}+\epsilon_{2})(1+2\epsilon_{2})\frac{||N||_{2}}{D}\;\;\textrm{ if }\epsilon_{2}&lt;0.5</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2(\epsilon_{1}+\epsilon_{2})\frac{||N||_{2}}{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2(\epsilon_{1}+\epsilon_{2})\frac{||N||_{2}}{D}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Why reducing bias in estimation is more important than reducing variance.</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The propagation of errors through the model can be modeled as a random walk of <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\pm\epsilon_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\pm\epsilon_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> steps for simplicity.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The argument follows from the standard analysis of mean-square error of random walk of <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> steps. Let each step have a mean square error of size <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">case 1: Entire MSE is attributed to bias</h4>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Then the MSE at step <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n^{2}\epsilon^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n^{2}\epsilon^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">case 2: Entire MSE is attributed to variance</h4>

<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Then the MSE at step <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\epsilon^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\epsilon^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, the impact of bias on error propagation is much stronger than that of variance.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Generally, if the bias and standard deviation of error at each step are <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu,\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu,\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, then the MSE at step <math id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A4.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MSE}(n)=n^{2}\mu^{2}+n\sigma^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>MSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MSE}(n)=n^{2}\mu^{2}+n\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A4.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{MSE}(n)=(n(n-1))\mu^{2}+n\epsilon^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>MSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{MSE}(n)=(n(n-1))\mu^{2}+n\epsilon^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Thus the compounding effect of bias is much stronger than that of variance.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Empirical Analysis of Tightness for CLT and Hoeffding Bounds</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present an empirical analysis of the tightness of our theoretical bounds for denominator approximation. We compare the Central Limit Theorem (CLT) based approximation with Hoeffding’s inequality, focusing on the configuration <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=0.1,\delta=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=0.1,\delta=0.2</annotation></semantics></math> with 5% oracle top-<math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> selection.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Summary analysis across layers</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The results are presented in Figure <a href="#A5.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ E.1 Summary analysis across layers ‣ Appendix E Empirical Analysis of Tightness for CLT and Hoeffding Bounds ‣ vAttention: Verified Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> and Figure <a href="#A5.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ E.1 Summary analysis across layers ‣ Appendix E Empirical Analysis of Tightness for CLT and Hoeffding Bounds ‣ vAttention: Verified Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluated the tightness of both bounds with the following setup:</p>
<ul id="A5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Approximation parameters</span>: <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=0.1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=0.2</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Oracle top-<math id="A5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math></span>: 5% of total tokens selected deterministically</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span>: Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct on RULER dataset with 16K context length</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.05688v1/images/clt_summary_eps_0.1_delta_0.2.png" id="A5.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:466/372;" width="466" height="372" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>CLT-based approximation analysis with <math id="A5.F11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=0.1,\delta=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=0.1,\delta=0.2</annotation></semantics></math> and 5% oracle top-<math id="A5.F11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A5.F12" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.05688v1/images/hoeffding_summary_eps_0.1_delta_0.2.png" id="A5.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:466/372;" width="466" height="372" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 12: </span>Hoeffding-based approximation analysis with <math id="A5.F12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=0.1,\delta=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=0.1,\delta=0.2</annotation></semantics></math> and 5% oracle top-<math id="A5.F12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, showing consistently higher sample requirements than CLT.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Comparing the two results (Figure <a href="#A5.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ E.1 Summary analysis across layers ‣ Appendix E Empirical Analysis of Tightness for CLT and Hoeffding Bounds ‣ vAttention: Verified Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> and Figure <a href="#A5.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ E.1 Summary analysis across layers ‣ Appendix E Empirical Analysis of Tightness for CLT and Hoeffding Bounds ‣ vAttention: Verified Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>) , we find:</p>
<ul id="A5.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A5.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conservative bounds</span>: Hoeffding equires 2.8× more samples (average 874) compared to CLT for the same guarantees.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A5.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A5.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Robust guarantees</span>: Hoeffing Achieves near-zero failure rate (<math id="A5.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;2\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;2\%</annotation></semantics></math>) but at significant computational cost.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Layer-Specific Analysis</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a given query, the distribution of attention scores <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{l,h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{l,h}</annotation></semantics></math> varies significantly across different heads/layers. The adaptive design of vAttention allows for dynamic budget for a given tolerance level <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon,\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon,\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>. Across different layers (layer 1/16/32) of the Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct model, we measure the empirical budget for the CLT and Hoeffding-based budget estimates. In particular, for <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon=0.1,\delta=0.2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon=0.1,\delta=0.2)</annotation></semantics></math>, we investigate the distribution of relative errors and average budget/head in Figures <a href="#A5.F13" title="Figure 13 ‣ E.2 Layer-Specific Analysis ‣ Appendix E Empirical Analysis of Tightness for CLT and Hoeffding Bounds ‣ vAttention: Verified Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> , <a href="#A5.F14" title="Figure 14 ‣ E.2 Layer-Specific Analysis ‣ Appendix E Empirical Analysis of Tightness for CLT and Hoeffding Bounds ‣ vAttention: Verified Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>,  <a href="#A5.F15" title="Figure 15 ‣ E.2 Layer-Specific Analysis ‣ Appendix E Empirical Analysis of Tightness for CLT and Hoeffding Bounds ‣ vAttention: Verified Sparse Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F13" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A5.F13.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.05688v1/images/clt_layer_001_eps_0.1_delta_0.2.png" id="A5.F13.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/362;" width="548" height="362" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span> <span id="A5.F13.sf1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CLT budget</span> : <span id="A5.F13.sf1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(top-left)</span> mean and maximum average relative error per head; the dashed line is the target error tolerance <math id="A5.F13.sf1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A5.F13.sf1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(top-right)</span> the fraction of queries <math id="A5.F13.sf1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\delta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\delta})</annotation></semantics></math> that are within the specified error tolerance <math id="A5.F13.sf1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A5.F13.sf1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(bottom-left)</span> vAttention budget per head with CLT relaxation <span id="A5.F13.sf1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(bottom-right)</span> distribution of relative errors (<math id="A5.F13.sf1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>) across heads </figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A5.F13.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.05688v1/images/hoeffding_layer_001_eps_0.1_delta_0.2.png" id="A5.F13.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/362;" width="548" height="362" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span><span id="A5.F13.sf2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hoeffding budget</span> : <span id="A5.F13.sf2.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(top-left)</span> mean and maximum average relative error per head; the dashed line is the target error tolerance <math id="A5.F13.sf2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A5.F13.sf2.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(top-right)</span> the fraction of queries <math id="A5.F13.sf2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\delta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\delta})</annotation></semantics></math> that are within the specified error tolerance <math id="A5.F13.sf2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A5.F13.sf2.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(bottom-left)</span> vAttention budget per head with Hoeffding bound <math id="A5.F13.sf2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{b}&lt;&lt;N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&lt;&lt;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{b}&lt;&lt;N</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A5.F13.sf2.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(bottom-right)</span> distribution of relative errors (<math id="A5.F13.sf2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>) across heads </figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 13: </span> <span id="A5.F13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Layer 1 analysis</span>: For early layers, the Hoeffding budget is non-vacuous and is highly likely to meet the verification thresholds. Further, the budget with CLT relaxation leads to much smaller budgets while providing a decent likelihood with average relative error within the tolerance error (<math id="A5.F13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>) </figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A5.F14" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A5.F14.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.05688v1/images/clt_layer_016_eps_0.1_delta_0.2.png" id="A5.F14.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/362;" width="548" height="362" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span> <span id="A5.F14.sf1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CLT budget</span> : <span id="A5.F14.sf1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(top-left)</span> mean and maximum average relative error per head; the dashed line is the target error tolerance <math id="A5.F14.sf1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A5.F14.sf1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(top-right)</span> the fraction of queries <math id="A5.F14.sf1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\delta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\delta})</annotation></semantics></math> that are within the specified error tolerance <math id="A5.F14.sf1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A5.F14.sf1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(bottom-left)</span> vAttention budget per head with CLT relaxation <span id="A5.F14.sf1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(bottom-right)</span> distribution of relative errors (<math id="A5.F14.sf1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>) across heads </figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A5.F14.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.05688v1/images/hoeffding_layer_016_eps_0.1_delta_0.2.png" id="A5.F14.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/362;" width="548" height="362" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span><span id="A5.F14.sf2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hoeffding budget</span> : <span id="A5.F14.sf2.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(top-left)</span> mean and maximum average relative error per head; the dashed line is the target error tolerance <math id="A5.F14.sf2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A5.F14.sf2.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(top-right)</span> the fraction of queries <math id="A5.F14.sf2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\delta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\delta})</annotation></semantics></math> that are within the specified error tolerance <math id="A5.F14.sf2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A5.F14.sf2.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(bottom-left)</span> vAttention budget per head with Hoeffding bound <math id="A5.F14.sf2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{b}&lt;&lt;N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&lt;&lt;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{b}&lt;&lt;N</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A5.F14.sf2.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(bottom-right)</span> distribution of relative errors (<math id="A5.F14.sf2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>) across heads </figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 14: </span> <span id="A5.F14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Layer 16 analysis</span>: For middle layers, the Hoeffding budget is more conservative and is requires high budget to meet the verification thresholds. Further, the budget with CLT relaxation leads to much smaller budgets while providing a decent likelihood with average relative error within the tolerance error (<math id="A5.F14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>), but have higher local errors </figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A5.F15" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A5.F15.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.05688v1/images/clt_layer_032_eps_0.1_delta_0.2.png" id="A5.F15.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/362;" width="548" height="362" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span> <span id="A5.F15.sf1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CLT budget</span> : <span id="A5.F15.sf1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(top-left)</span> mean and maximum average relative error per head; the dashed line is the target error tolerance <math id="A5.F15.sf1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A5.F15.sf1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(top-right)</span> the fraction of queries <math id="A5.F15.sf1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\delta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\delta})</annotation></semantics></math> that are within the specified error tolerance <math id="A5.F15.sf1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A5.F15.sf1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(bottom-left)</span> vAttention budget per head with CLT relaxation <span id="A5.F15.sf1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(bottom-right)</span> distribution of relative errors (<math id="A5.F15.sf1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>) across heads </figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A5.F15.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2510.05688v1/images/hoeffding_layer_032_eps_0.1_delta_0.2.png" id="A5.F15.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/362;" width="548" height="362" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span><span id="A5.F15.sf2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hoeffding budget</span> : <span id="A5.F15.sf2.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(top-left)</span> mean and maximum average relative error per head; the dashed line is the target error tolerance <math id="A5.F15.sf2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A5.F15.sf2.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(top-right)</span> the fraction of queries <math id="A5.F15.sf2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\hat{\delta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>δ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\hat{\delta})</annotation></semantics></math> that are within the specified error tolerance <math id="A5.F15.sf2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A5.F15.sf2.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(bottom-left)</span> vAttention budget per head with Hoeffding bound <math id="A5.F15.sf2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{b}&lt;&lt;N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&lt;&lt;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{b}&lt;&lt;N</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A5.F15.sf2.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(bottom-right)</span> distribution of relative errors (<math id="A5.F15.sf2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>) across heads </figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 15: </span> <span id="A5.F15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Layer 32 analysis</span>: For late layers, the Hoeffding budget is less likely to meet verification thresholds. Further, the budget with CLT relaxation leads to much smaller budgets while providing a decent likelihood with average relative error within the tolerance error (<math id="A5.F15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>)</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
